        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "746d2301-ae65-5b63-b7bd-8d257d8cbe4b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Josef Hirsch Janow, Raphael Kohn, Salomon Maimon\n- Roles: Rabbi, philosopher\n- Places: Posen, Fürth, Hamburg, Altona, Wandsbeck, present-day Belarus\n- Concepts: Talmudical discussions, benevolence\n\nFacts:\n- Josef Hirsch Janow was born in 1733 and died on 13 November 1785.\n- Salomon Maimon was born in 1753 and died on 22 November 1800.\n- Salomon Maimon was a German-speaking philosopher born to Jewish parents in present-day Belarus.\n- Josef Hirsch Janow was a Polish rabbi who was commonly called \"Hirsch Ḥarif\" because of his keenness in Talmudical discussions.\n- In 1776, when Raphael Kohn was elected rabbi of the three congregations of Hamburg, Altona, and Wandsbeck, Josef Hirsch Janow succeeded him as rabbi of Posen.\n- In 1777, Josef Hirsch Janow was called to the rabbinate of Fürth.\n- In his \"Lebensgeschichte,\" Salomon Maimon highly praised Josef Hirsch Janow for his benevolence.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6f1c2056-c965-54c0-893b-11338127312f",
        "text": "Page: Hirsch Janow. Sentence: Josef Hirsch Janow (1733 – 13 November 1785) was a Polish rabbi, who, on account of his great keenness in Talmudical discussions, was commonly called \"\"Hirsch Ḥarif\"\" (the acute).\nPage: Hirsch Janow. Sentence: When in 1776 his father-in-law, Raphael Kohn, was elected rabbi of the 3 congregations Hamburg, Altona, and Wandsbeck, he succeeded him as rabbi of Posen.\nPage: Hirsch Janow. Sentence: In the following year he was called to the rabbinate of Fürth.\nPage: Hirsch Janow. Sentence: Salomon Maimon, in his \"Lebensgeschichte\" (pp 280 et seq.), highly praises Hirsch Janow for his benevolence.\nPage: Salomon Maimon. Sentence: Salomon Maimon ( ; ] ; Hebrew: שלמה מימון‎ ‎ ‎; 1753 – 22 November 1800) was a German-speaking philosopher, born of Jewish parentage in present-day Belarus.",
